<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    structsynth: synthesize a structure type from the constant-offset
    dereferences of a pointer parameter.

    Source shape (hand-assembled, no prologue, so the parameter arrives in RDI
    with nothing declaring its type):

        int two_fields(void *p) {
            unsigned char *s = *(unsigned char **)p;   // offset 0, 8 bytes
            int n = *(int *)((char *)p + 8);           // offset 8, 4 bytes
            return n + *s;
        }

        48 8b 07        mov    rax,[rdi]
        8b 4f 08        mov    ecx,[rdi+8]
        0f b6 00        movzx  eax,byte [rax]
        01 c8           add    eax,ecx
        c3              ret

    The dereference at offset 0 is what makes RDI a pointer to type inference;
    `structsynth` never invents pointer-ness, so a parameter the engine still
    believes is an integer is left alone.

    Default (assert #1): the two reads are raw offset arithmetic over an
    untyped pointee, and the reader carries the layout in their head.

    With `option structsynth param` (asserts 2 to 6): once type propagation has
    settled, the two constant offsets are completed into `struct_0` and the
    parameter is type-locked to `struct_0 *`, so both reads render as fields and
    the recovered layout is printable.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
488b078b4f080fb60001c8c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="two_fields"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>lo fu two_fields</com>
  <com>option structsynth off</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option structsynth param</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>print C types</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="STRUCTSYNTH #1: default leaves the offset-8 read as raw pointer arithmetic" min="1" max="1">\*\(int4 \*\)&amp;a0\[1\]</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="STRUCTSYNTH #2: the parameter is retyped to the synthesized structure" min="1" max="1">struct_0 \*a0</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="STRUCTSYNTH #3: the offset-8 read renders as a field" min="1" max="1">a0-&gt;field_0x8</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="STRUCTSYNTH #4: the offset-0 read renders as a field" min="1" max="1">a0-&gt;field_0x0</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="STRUCTSYNTH #5: offset 0 keeps the pointer type its loaded value carries" min="1" max="1">uint1 \*field_0x0;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="STRUCTSYNTH #6: offset 8 is a 4-byte field, not a padded 8-byte one" min="1" max="1">int4 field_0x8;</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
